  "screenwriter_raw": "{\n  \"pseudos\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"p1\",\n      \"text\": \"The casting of Lupita Nyong'o as Helen of Troy and Clytemnestra in Christopher Nolan's upcoming Homer adaptation has drawn waves of targeted harassment online. This public accusation by prominent commentators, framing the move as a threat to European history, has created a painful public ordeal for the performer facing public backlash. The resulting cultural controversy has transformed a mythic epic into a flashpoint over identity, illustrating how a creative project can become a site of injury for the individual at its center.\",\n      \"fit\": 0.91,\n      \"center\": \"who-1\",\n      \"channel\": \"toned\",\n      \"source\": {\n        \"fragments\": [\"how-0\", \"how-1\", \"how-2\", \"result-0\"]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"p2\",\n      \"text\": \"A fierce digital backlash erupted after the casting announcement, with an outpouring of online hostility targeting the film production. Defenders argued that diverse casting treats the Western canon as shared civilizational heritage, making a case for artistic inclusion. This ideological conflict, a public dispute over narrative ownership, shows how the production team found itself caught in a societal debate that extends far beyond the film itself, demanding a response to protect the creative project under fire.\",\n      \"fit\": 0.85,\n      \"center\": \"who-4\",\n      \"channel\": \"toned\",\n      \"source\": {\n        \"fragments\": [\"how-0\", \"how-1\", \"how-3\", \"result-0\", \"result-1\"]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"p3\",\n      \"text\": \"The filmmaker at the center of the controversy faces an escalation of cultural tensions following the casting decision. Prominent commentators, acting as public figures stoking controversy with inflammatory rhetoric, have fueled a social media conflict. Supporters of the casting decision countered with a defense statement, arguing for inclusive storytelling. This has left the film director navigating a harmful public debate where the production's creative choices have become the focus of a wider cultural claim over who may tell these stories.\",\n      \"fit\": 0.78,\n      \"center\": \"who-0\",\n      \"channel\": \"toned\",\n      \"source\": {\n        \"fragments\": [\"how-0\", \"how-1\", \"how-2\", \"how-3\", \"result-1\"]\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}",
